- Added `name` and `description` fields to configuration profiles, and replaced the add and edit profile modals with a page where the profile's contents can be pasted or edited inline. Admins can set the name and description in the UI, through the API (`name` and `description` on the create, update and batch endpoints, with `display_name` on the batch endpoint deprecated in favor of `name`) and in GitOps YAML. A replacement file no longer renames the profile unless `name` is sent. Changing the name or description doesn't re-send the profile to hosts. The one exception is renaming a Windows, Android, or declaration (DDM) profile through GitOps, which re-creates the profile, so hosts install it again. The list and get endpoints return `description`, and `payload_display_name` for `.mobileconfig` profiles.
